[{"id":3656295918,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7Z7qXu","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?u=af70f5d107e9c1447f296643d5a566dab53d25e8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114922#pullrequestreview-3656295918","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114922","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114922#pullrequestreview-3656295918"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114922"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-13T15:03:00Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3658442729,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7aD2fp","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?u=5f2b0cb28e37393252e96695f2eaa33494930285&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@DarioSamo This is a good start but I'd like to consolidate and cleanup the logic to decide which renderer / fallback to use as at the moment it's still split between the Android and native code. The [code is as follow](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/481f36ed20520db3195a09cc309abf48c03cf51a/platform/android/java/lib/src/main/java/org/godotengine/godot/Godot.kt#L568-L581):\n```\n\t\t\trenderView = if (usesVulkan()) {\n\t\t\t\tif (meetsVulkanRequirements(context.packageManager)) {\n\t\t\t\t\tGodotVulkanRenderView(this, godotInputHandler, shouldBeTransparent)\n\t\t\t\t} else if (canFallbackToOpenGL()) {\n\t\t\t\t\t// Fallback to OpenGl.\n\t\t\t\t\tGodotGLRenderView(this, godotInputHandler, xrMode, useDebugOpengl, shouldBeTransparent)\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tthrow IllegalStateException(context.getString(R.string.error_missing_vulkan_requirements_message))\n\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t// Fallback to OpenGl.\n\t\t\t\tGodotGLRenderView(this, godotInputHandler, xrMode, useDebugOpengl, shouldBeTransparent)\n\t\t\t}\n```\nwhere `usesVulkan()` invokes `GodotLib.getRendererInfo()` which in this PR invokes the new logic you added. Things work as expected if either:\n- the renderer is set to vulkan, the new check cannot init vulkan and opengl fallback is enabled, in which case `GodotLib.getRendererInfo()` returns `opengl` and we fall to the last `else` block\n- the renderer is set to opengl in which case we fall to the last `else` block as well\n\nHowever we have edge cases in the following scenarios:\n- the renderer is set to vulkan, opengl fallback is not enabled and the new check cannot init vulkan; in this scenario `usesVulkan()` will still return `true`, and we'll attempt to proceed until `DisplayServerAndroid` fails when it tries to initialize. Instead we should fail early and fast. This can be done by updating the return value of `usesVulkan` so we can differentiate this scenario from the others.\n- the renderer is set to vulkan and the new check can init vulkan properly (-> `usesVulkan()` returns `true`) but (somehow) `meetsVulkanRequirements(...)` returns `false`. This scenario has two cases to consider:\n  - between `meetsVulkanRequirements(...)` and the new check, which takes precedence? As in do we ignore the value of `meetsVulkanRequirements(...)` if we are able to init the vulkan context, or do we skip trying to init the vulkan context if `meetsVulkanRequirements(...)` returns false.\n  - In the current logic, if `meetsVulkanRequirements(...)` returns `false`, and opengl fallback is enabled, we proceed with the GL surface without updating the rendering driver with the expectation that `DisplayServerAndroid` will fail to init vulkan and also switch to opengl. However as mentioned in the above point, if we are somehow able to init vulkan, we now have a vulkan context attempting to run on a GL surface.\n\nIdeally, we should consolidate the logic so that `usesVulkan()` (renamed to `getNativeRenderer()`, or more appropriate name,  in the pseudocode below) behaves as such:\n```\n\t\t\tval nativeRenderer = getNativeRenderer()\n\t\t\trenderView = if (nativeRenderer == VULKAN) {\n\t\t\t\t\tGodotVulkanRenderView(this, godotInputHandler, shouldBeTransparent)\n\t\t\t\t} else if (nativeRenderer == OPENGL) {\n\t\t\t\t\tGodotGLRenderView(this, godotInputHandler, xrMode, useDebugOpengl, shouldBeTransparent)\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tthrow IllegalStateException(context.getString(R.string.error_missing_vulkan_requirements_message))\n\t\t\t\t}\n```\n\nWith the updated `usesVulkan()` / `getNativeRenderer()` behaving as follow:\n- if the renderer is set to opengl, returns OPENGL\n- if the renderer is set to vulkan AND meets the vulkan requirements AND vulkan context can be initialized, return VULKAN\n- if the renderer is set to vulkan AND (does not meet the vulkan requirements OR vulkan context cannot be initialized):\n  - if opengl fallback is enabled, return OPENGL\n  - else return a value to indicate failure\n\nI think we can have this logic in the native code and have the Android code invoke it. Checking the vulkan requirements use Android specific APIs so we'll either need to pass a value to indicate the result of the check to the native function, or set up a jni method so the native code can invoke the relevant Android APIs.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114922#pullrequestreview-3658442729","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114922","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114922#pullrequestreview-3658442729"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114922"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-14T00:51:55Z","commit_id":"e6ed31b75a29121423badf0aea742b731cf5dadf"},{"id":3663147564,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7aVzIs","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?u=5f2b0cb28e37393252e96695f2eaa33494930285&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.gi